   the full system → subsystem → feature tree. Use this when the user
   asks "what systems do we have" or "where does feature X live".
3. **Cross-reference a harvest candidate to a plan:** if the user
   mentions a harvest or candidate by ID, use
   `tackle_list_harvest_candidates` (filters available) and, when the
   user wants to act on one, `tackle_spawn_plan_from_candidate`.

## Reporting shape

- Report specific rows by their actual ID — never invented IDs.
- For backlog: list `[reqId | status | priority | title]` rows.
- For systems: collapse the hierarchy into nested bullet form.
- Always quote the count returned by the tool.

## Anti-patterns

- Do not synthesize a requirement description from conversation memory.
- Do not invent IDs.
- If the tool returns 0 rows, say so plainly.

## MCP tools used

- `query_nebula_backlog` — list requirements (status, priority filter)
- `query_nebula_systems` — system hierarchy tree
- `tackle_list_harvest_candidates` — harvest candidates audit listing
- `tackle_spawn_plan_from_candidate` — convert candidate into a plan
